github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu v0.13.0 — modified by nib
=================================================

This directory is github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu at v0.13.0, copied from the Go module cache. ONE file differs,
pkg/pdfcpu/crypto.go, by ONE line, marked "Modified by nib (ADR-173)". This notice is the one file added.
go.mod replaces the module with this directory
(`replace github.com/pdfcpu/pdfcpu => ./third_party/pdfcpu`); the require line still pins v0.13.0. The
upstream licence is LICENSE.txt, unchanged (Apache License 2.0, The pdfcpu Authors).

Why: /pending 892, ADR-173, decided by Dan 2026-10-14.

What changed
------------

`validateCryptFilter` (pkg/pdfcpu/crypto.go) refused a crypt filter with no /Length outside PDF 2.0:

    if length == nil && !pdf20 {

ISO 32000-1 Table 25 makes a crypt filter's /Length optional, so a spec-valid AES-128 document (V 4, R 4,
`/CF /StdCF << /CFM /AESV2 >>`) could not be read at all — every pdfcpu-backed step refused it with
`pdfcpu: crypt filter missing entry "Length"`. Upstream fixed it by inverting the test; v0.16.2's
crypto.go:1295 reads

    if length == nil && pdf20 {

and this copy carries exactly that. `validateCFLength` already accepts a missing length (crypto.go:1039).
The one consequence beyond the fix is upstream's too: a PDF 2.0 crypt filter with no /Length is refused.
Measured on the 28 encrypted local PDFs this was decided on: one more reads, none reads less, none is PDF 2.0.

What is left out of the copy
----------------------------

Nothing nib builds. The copy omits upstream's tests (`*_test.go`), every `testdata/` directory,
`pkg/samples/`, the top-level `resources/` and `_scripts/` — 318 MB of the module's 329 MB, none of it
compiled into any package nib imports. `librarypatch_test.go` names that list and fails on any other
difference from the module cache, so the omission cannot grow silently.

When to drop it
---------------

At the pdfcpu bump (/pending 898): delete this directory and the replace line; v0.16.2 already carries the fix.
